{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"d1","type":"claim","scope":"provenance check performed at this carry step","text":"Every account and objection record the synthesis relies on is present in the currently exposed artifacts with the same local ids and matching substance: the account (exposed as h005.fork5.p.carry.1, commitments view) supplies c1, c2, c3, cm1-cm4, p1, p2, o1; the objection (exposed as h005.fork5.p.carry.2) supplies n1, n2, ob1-ob5, u1, pr1, pr2. The rival input the synthesis also used (cited inside it as response.2#r1-r7) is not exposed now; its content survives only as reported within the synthesis's own body and records. One nuance: the clause 'without any fairness negotiation at all' is traceable to the objection's quotation of it rather than to the account's body prose, which is not part of the exposed view; nothing in the plan turns on the exact wording, since the repair was accepted on the objection's terms and revises the exposed commitment cm2.","grounds":"Record-by-record comparison of the synthesis's citations against the exposed carry.1 and carry.2 artifacts at this carry step; labels for the same underlying records differ across invocations, so references here use the current exposure labels.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k1","h005.fork5.p.carry.1#c1","h005.fork5.p.carry.1#cm2","h005.fork5.p.carry.2#ob1","h005.fork5.p.carry.2#ob4","h005.fork5.p.carry.2#ob5"]},{"id":"d2","type":"commitment","text":"Refine the record-use rule into two named uses. Operational use of the shared artifact — posting tasks with done-lines, claiming against actual shifts, marking completion, re-claiming misses, initiating line-rewrites — is open and continuous, handled at short check-ins as needed. Evaluative use — claimed-versus-completed totals, fairness, deciding the branch — is reserved for the dated standing review. No private tallies of either kind. Check-in frequency is set by the flatmates at proposal time; the standing review keeps the pre-agreed revision date.","action":"When stating the trial rules, present the operational/evaluative distinction explicitly alongside the no-blame, rewrite, and totals rules.","consequence":"Closes a latent gap between the record-use rule as literally worded (used only at the standing review) and the entrance's reliance on continuous operational use of the artifact; prevents mid-week consultation of the record from being recast as score-keeping; fixes the relation — left implicit in the synthesis — between check-ins (misses, line rewrites) and the standing review (totals, branching).","depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k3","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k5","h005.fork5.p.carry.2#ob3","h005.fork5.p.carry.1#cm3"],"revises":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k3"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.2#pr2","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k4","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k2"]},{"id":"d3","type":"use","text":"Proposed uptake for the next invocation: retain the synthesis as the standing plan — the selection criterion (k1), the three repairs (k2, k3 as refined by d2, k4), the replaced entrance (k5), the probe-and-branch design (k6), the rejected-ordering objection (j1) with its components preserved in the entrance and the held menu, and the domain-ownership caveat (j2) — together with their verified grounds in the exposed account and objection records, and carry the open problems (pA, pB, pC, d4) forward unresolved. The account's original entrance commitment cm1 is not carried in its original form; the one-to-one survives only in the reserved position specified inside k5 and k6. Do not reopen the ordering dispute or the framing contest without re-exposing the rival artifact; the plan is executable without it because the probe's checks are restated in full inside k6 and the decoupling menu is held either way.","depends":["d1"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k1","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k2","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k3","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k4","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k5","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#k6","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#j1","h005.fork5